{
  "id": "truth-bias",
  "term": "truth bias",
  "definition": "Truth bias is the common tendency to judge other people’s messages as true rather than deceptive, even in settings where deception is possible. It reflects a greater reluctance to wrongly label a truthful message as a lie than to miss a lie.",
  "field": "learning",
